  era: "c. 1573 onward \xB7 Section 16 \xB7 Mughal Empire \xB7 1526 \u2013 1857"
  title: Mansabdari system
  text: Akbar's mansabdari system ranked every officer by zat, personal rank, and sawar, the number of cavalry to be maintained. Mansabdars were usually paid through jagirs, assignments of land revenue that were transferred to prevent local power bases.
